// MIR → JS emission (D-43): direct-style strict CBPV onto a JS subset.
// ret / roll / unroll / parens / annotations are transparent; leaves map
// 1:1. JS has one expression sort, so no coercion happens here.

// Extern rules (D-01/D-38) host what derived rules cannot express —
// singleton parameter lists, argument/arm folds, and ident → "string"
// quoting (tags, cap names):
//   thunk_lambda — ThunkV `() => c`, LamC `(x) => c`
//   force_apply  — ForceC `v()`, CompPostfix `c(args…)`
//   let_fix      — LetC `((x) => b)(c)`, FixC `function f() { return c; }()`
//   case_arms    — CaseC as nested ternaries over `s.$ === "Tag"`,
//                  binders as IIFEs over `s.args[i]`, else
//                  `__lumo_match_error(s)`
//   ctor_bundle  — CtorV `({ $: "Tag", args: […] })`, BundleV
//                  `({ op: (p, q) => c })` (object literals are always
//                  parenthesized — an arrow body `{…}` would read as a
//                  block in real JS)
//   caps         — PerformC `__lumo_perform("C")`, HandleC
//                  `__lumo_handle("C", h, () => b)` (D-43 runtime);
//                  TryC `__lumo_boundary((k) => b)`, AbortC
//                  `__lumo_abort(k, v)` (D-54 boundary)
extern rule thunk_lambda from MIR to JS
extern rule force_apply from MIR to JS
extern rule let_fix from MIR to JS
extern rule case_arms from MIR to JS
extern rule ctor_bundle from MIR to JS
extern rule caps from MIR to JS

from MIR to JS {
  File { defs: [$d*] } ==> JS::File { stmts: [$d* to JS] }
  Def { name: $n, value: $v } ==> ConstDecl { name: $n, value: $v to JS }

  VarV { name: $n } ==> IdentExpr { name: $n }
  NumV { value: $v } ==> NumExpr { value: $v }
  StrV { value: $v } ==> StrExpr { value: $v }

  // F-intro, iso-recursion and grouping are erased: JS is untyped and
  // the builders re-parenthesize by precedence.
  RetC { value: $v } ==> $v to JS
  RollV { value: $v } ==> $v to JS
  UnrollV { value: $v } ==> $v to JS
  ParenV { inner: $v } ==> $v to JS
  ParenC { inner: $c } ==> $c to JS

  SelC { value: $v, field: $f }
    ==> ExprPostfix { op: '.', expr: $v to JS, member_name: MemberName { name: $f } }
}
